// ============================================================
// THE SUPER — three combos land, and the next swing is not a swing
//
// What it pays in, and why it is not a bigger hit. NOTES has the ceiling written down:
// taps are 4–7% of total impact, so doubling or tripling a swing could never feel worth a
// build-up. So the super pays in the two currencies the world layer already uses:
//   1. the road — every trouble on it goes down at once, each leaving what it was holding,
//      which is worth up to the −30% they were taking off production;
//   2. a short window where the street works with you, ×superMult for superSeg seconds,
//      applied exactly where the mutirão is applied.
// What gates it is NOT the combo count — nine swings is 1.3s while holding. It is
// `superRecarga`: after it fires, combos stop counting for 22s. That makes the super a
// once-every-~23s event whether you are holding the button or poking at it, which is what
// lets the payoff be tuned as a per-23s thing.
//
// The rule the whole file obeys: **it does not touch tiredness, in either direction.**
// Not the emission, not the decay, not a heal. The one shape this game has already died
// of is automation that pays down tiredness.
//
