  // the team recovers while you organise together, not while you burn them out:
  // healing only in GO STEADY is what keeps holding the button from erasing tiredness.
  // A shot the wand fires by itself is not people helping each other, so it never heals —
  // that keeps automatic output structurally incapable of paying for GO FAST.
  // The combo counter advances for EVERY swing, auto-helpers included, so reach and damage
  // are unchanged and the economy sim stays byte-identical (it models neither jumpT nor
  // attackType). But only a REAL tap moves the hero: the neighbours' auto-taps (U4, 2/s) and
  // the wand skill used to drive the whole 3-hit combo, so the character leapt on its own
  // every ~1.5s and the frame read as bugged in production. The visible swing and leap now
  // fire on player taps only; the auto-helpers still deal their damage below.
  // Owner: the leap comes on every FIFTH swing, not every third. Four ordinary casts, then
  // she goes up.
  const PASSOS = 5, SALTO = PASSOS - 1;
