// mobLuz were retired when the troubles became authored sprite frames — see MOB_B64, MOB_SPR,
// mobFrame and drawMobs above. The intro postcard keeps its own tiny SMOG_MINI cut.
// ---- foliage: canopies with volume, baked once ----
// Three stacked rectangles and a dozen random stipple pixels never read as a tree with a
// lit side and a shaded side. These are hand-shaded maps — deep shadow into the lower left,
// base green through the middle, light and a rim on the upper right where the sun is —
// baked like the characters, so a whole forest costs one drawImage each.
// THE BIG STREET TREE'S FIVE GREENS, HAZED. Turning that tree off is the cleanest
// attribution in this file: it buys the whole of the wave-11 framing (visible open sky
// 34.9% -> 31.2%, CEU baixo 61.1% -> 50.1%, y86-107 dE 9.1 -> 12.5) and it charges the
// hero croma 73 -> 149 of 485 at MANHÃ, dE 29 -> 40, luma 35 -> 49. The framing is worth
// keeping and the bill is not, and the two come apart, because what rivals him is not the
// tree's MASS — a flat mass scores near zero, which is the whole reason the framing measure
// had to be rewritten in wave 11 — it is the tree's SATURATION standing against open sky.
// So the mass stays to the pixel and the colour steps back one plane: this crown is the one
// green in the picture with nothing but sky behind it, which is exactly the thing aerial
// perspective acts on. Same five colours, same construction, one desaturation, done once at
// load and in BASE colours so `wc` still applies the hour exactly once.
// A MIX TOWARD BRILHO WAS THE FIRST CUT AND THE PRINT REFUSED IT. It measured well — at 0.42
// his croma went 149 -> 100 — but it works by LIGHTENING, so the crown came out paler than
// the ridges behind it, and a near tree paler than the far hill inverts the depth of the
// whole picture. This is the same move with the value left alone: each colour is pulled
// toward its own Rec.709 luma, so the crown stays exactly as dark against the sky as it was
