// The wand is an ordinary thing: a branch someone worked a little and bound at one end.
// It is NOT an artefact — at rest it gives off no light at all, which is what lets a cast
// be an event. Three things keep it from reading as a log, which it used to: it is walked
// one pixel at a time and drawn in three passes (outline, body, sunlit side) so a diagonal
// stays a stick; it **tapers**, two pixels thick at the grip down to one at the tip; and it
// **bows** slightly across its span, because a branch that is perfectly straight is a dowel.
// `brilho` is the charge, and it is only ever non-zero while he is casting.
// ---------- BASTÃO — CETRO DA VIDA ----------
// The board gives this object a name and a page of its own: "feito de madeira, memória e
// esperança". A worked branch, bound in cord that spirals up the shaft, carrying a spoked
// wooden wheel at the top with a warm core, leaves growing straight off the rim, and cords
// hanging under it with beads and a crystal. It is drawn, not sprited, because it has to
// follow the arm through a swing and a full front flip.
//
// The wheel is baked once per (radius, glow step) into an offscreen canvas: it is thirty-odd
// fillRects and it would otherwise be paid on every frame of every swing.
// (The CETRO staff palette and its procedural wheel/shaft renderer were retired with the
// procedural hero; the authored sprite frames carry the staff now.)
// ---------- THE HOUR, ON THE HERO ----------
// He was the one thing in the frame drawn in fixed colours, so at midnight he stood in the
// street lit as if it were noon — a cut-out pasted onto the picture. He takes the hour now,
// but not the same dose the world takes, because two things have to survive it:
//   · HE HAS TO STAY READABLE AT PHONE SIZE. The world's dimming (`escala`, 0.44 at NOITE)
//     would sink a 22 px character into the ground plane. His is FLOORED — a third of the
//     way back to full — and the hour's tint reaches him at 80% strength, so night moves
//     him a long way in hue and only a little in value. He goes cool and quiet; he never
//     goes to a silhouette.
//   · THE CETRO STAYS THE BRIGHTEST THING IN A DARK FRAME. Its wood takes an even gentler
//     dose (floored more than half way, tint at 45%), and the lit hub, the crystal and
//     everything `luz()` draws are not touched by the hour at all. So as the street goes
//     down around him, the staff's share of the frame's light goes UP, which is the read
//     the direction asks for: the Cetro is the light source, not a lit object.
// Both are resolved on 24 steps of the day and the hero's sprite is re-baked on the step,
// so a normal frame is still one drawImage and a handful of cached colour strings.
function hexA(s) { return [parseInt(s.substr(1, 2), 16), parseInt(s.substr(3, 2), 16), parseInt(s.substr(5, 2), 16)]; }
function luzPersonagem(c, piso, forcaF, recupC?) {
  const q = horaAgora();
  const esc = lerp(lerp(q.a.escala, q.b.escala, q.f), 1, piso);
  const forca = lerp(q.a.forca, q.b.forca, q.f) * forcaF;
  const tin = mixA(q.a.tinta, q.b.tinta, q.f);
  const m = mixA([cl255(c[0] * esc), cl255(c[1] * esc), cl255(c[2] * esc)], tin, forca);
  if (!recupC) return m;
  // THE TINT DOES NOT ONLY COOL HIM, IT FLATTENS HIM. Mixing every pigment he owns toward
  // ONE colour pulls them all to the same point in a*b*, so at NOITE, tinted 80%, he ended
  // up at C* 7.4 against 9.9 for the street around him — measured in wave 9, and the frame
  // has only got greener since. Less saturated than his own background is the wrong picture
  // for the one character in it, and the obvious fix — tint him less — is the one wave 7
  // already refused with a number, because it is his VALUE at night that makes him read as
  // somebody standing in the dark.
  // So the two are separated. The mix keeps the hour's hue and the hour's value exactly as
  // they were, and then the residual chroma is re-expanded ABOUT HIS OWN LUMA — which is a
  // pure saturation move: Rec.709 luma of the result is unchanged (the expansion is applied
  // to c − y, and the weights of that vector sum to zero), so the poncho stays where wave 7
  // measured it. Only where the tint actually bit, in proportion to how hard it bit, which
  // is why MANHÃ comes out identical to the pixel.
  // It costs him one point of luma contrast at NOITE (21.9 → 20.9, rank 66 → 80 of 485) and
  // I could not explain that away: capping the factor per colour so no channel can clip —
  // the expansion is luma-neutral only while nothing clamps — changed the number by 0.0, so
  // it is not clipping, and the same point was lost at 0.65 as at 1.05. Kept anyway, because
  // dE is what the eye actually gets and dE goes 45 → 34 while croma goes 63 → 32.
  // ...and a FLOOR under it, which is this wave's correction. The expansion above only ever
  // fired where the tint bit, so at MANHÃ (forca 0.04) it did nothing at all and his chroma
  // was whatever the raw palette gave: C* 23.5, fixed, while the street around him went from
  // C* 15.8 to 18.0 as this wave gave the sky, the haze and the stone back their colour. He
  // did not get duller; the field caught up, and his chroma rank fell 83 -> 201 of 485 for it.
  // The direction has said from the first line that HE DOES NOT DESATURATE WITH THE WORLD, so
  // the floor is the direction written down: a constant about his own luma, in every
  // hour, luma-neutral by the same argument as the term beside it.
  // IT HAS BEEN RAISED THREE TIMES AND ALWAYS FOR THE SAME REASON — 1.32 in wave 13, 1.50 in
  // wave 15, 1.70 here — and the reason is never that he got duller, it is that the street
  // caught up. Wave 19 gave the proscenium its chroma back and took the frame from C* 18.3
  // to 19.5, which is the board; his ratio against it fell 1.52 -> 1.43 in the same breath.
  // At 1.70 it is 1.50 at MANHÃ and 1.19 at NOITE, his MANHÃ croma rank is 70 of 485 against
  // the 103 the wave opened on, and his NOITE ranks are 40 / 4 / 1 against 40 / 8 / 3.
  // Above this the expansion starts to CLIP: 1.78 measured C* 31.3 where the pure ratio
  // wants 32.7, and clipping is what breaks the luma-neutrality the whole move rests on —
  // the poncho reads 123.3 at NOITE instead of 123.4, and his NOITE luma rank goes 40 -> 43.
  // One tenth of a luma and three ranks is the price of this floor and it is written here
  // rather than left for someone to find.
  const y = 0.2126 * m[0] + 0.7152 * m[1] + 0.0722 * m[2], k = 1.70 + recupC * forca;
  return [cl255(y + (m[0] - y) * k), cl255(y + (m[1] - y) * k), cl255(y + (m[2] - y) * k)];
}
// (The per-hour hero/staff colour bake — heroLuzPasso, hc, cc, rodaCanvas, vara —
// was retired with the procedural hero. luzPersonagem above stays: the world uses it.
function drawHero() {
  // ---- pick the animation from existing state, in priority order ----
  // 1) airborne (third-hit leap / attackType 2)  -> special sequence
  // 2) casting (attackType 0/1)                  -> atk1 / atk2
  // 3) otherwise                                 -> the run cycle (walk-by-default)
  const air = jumpT > 0;
  const pj = air ? 1 - jumpT / JUMPF : 0;                 // 0 = take-off, 1 = landing
  const alto = air ? Math.round(Math.pow(Math.sin(pj * Math.PI), 0.7) * 52) : 0;  // the leap arc
  const bx = HX - 8, y0 = GROUND - 44 - alto;             // kept only as the bolt spawn origin
  const mid = HX;                                         // his centre line / feet x
  let frames, fi;
  if (air) {
    // A real jump cycle now: crouch, push off, rise, apex, fall, land. It replaced the SUPER
    // frames that used to sit here and set off a green blast in mid-air. The sheet was drawn
    // 1.54x larger than the walk one (measured on head width, the one thing that does not move
    // with the pose), so it was resampled to match before being embedded.
    frames = heroBloco("sp");
    fi = Math.max(0, Math.min(frames.length - 1, Math.floor((1 - jumpT / JUMPF) * frames.length)));
  } else if (attackT > 0 && attackType === 0) {
    frames = heroBloco("atk1");
    fi = Math.max(0, Math.min(frames.length - 1, Math.floor((1 - attackT / ATKF) * frames.length)));
  } else if (attackT > 0 && attackType === 1) {
    frames = heroBloco("atk2");
    fi = Math.max(0, Math.min(frames.length - 1, Math.floor((1 - attackT / ATKF) * frames.length)));
  } else if (obraTrabalhando) {
    // A POSE DE QUEM TRABALHA é a MESMA de quem mora na faixa (atk1, quadro 3): gesto de quem
    // segura o que trouxe, nunca de quem golpeia — e essa distinção é o §2, não estética.
    // Sem este ramo a caminhada CONGELARIA no quadro em que estava, porque o quadro é escolhido
    // por distância e a distância parou: meia passada parada no ar, que lê como travamento.
    frames = heroBloco("atk1");
    fi = Math.min(3, frames.length - 1);
  } else {
    // The frame is picked by DISTANCE covered, not by elapsed time, so the stride can never
    // drift out of step with the ground however fast the street is moving. GO FAST has its own
    // twelve poses and its own, longer stride — it is a run, not the walk hurried along.
    const correndo = S.modo === "carvao" && temCorrida();
    // O MESMO passo que `velocidadeMundo()` usa, pela MESMA função. Antes esta linha lia
    // `passoCap().passo` fixo: com uma folha de corrida ligada, o quadro seria escolhido a cada
    // passo da CAMINHADA enquanto o chão andava no passo da CORRIDA, e a sola arrastaria a
    // diferença inteira. É a armadilha nº 1 do §7 pela porta dos fundos.
    const passo = passoAgora();
    frames = correndo ? heroBloco("run") : heroBloco("walk");
    // o módulo é o TAMANHO DO CICLO, não um 12 fixo: a caminhada do capítulo 1 tem três quadros
    const n = frames.length;
    fi = n ? ((Math.floor(worldX / passo) % n) + n) % n : 0;
  }
  const img = frames[fi];

  // contact shadow: stays on the ground and tightens as he climbs, which sells the leap
  sombra(mid, GROUND, Math.max(9, 28 - Math.round(alto * 0.34)), Math.max(0.07, 0.32 - alto * 0.0045));

  // The magic bolt is spawned off the swing state exactly as before, so the decorative bolt
  // that leaves the wand is untouched by the sprite rewrite. A new swing = attackT jumped up
  // or attackType stepped on.
  if (attackT > 0 && (attackT > ultAtkT || attackType !== ultAtkTipo)) lancarMagia(attackType, bx, y0);
  ultAtkT = attackT; ultAtkTipo = attackType;
  flashCast = Math.max(0, flashCast - 0.11);              // the cast charge burns off

  // Feet-anchored: the sprite's bottom-centre sits at (HX, GROUND - lift). She is blitted on
  // her own device-resolution canvas rather than into the low-res world, so the art is scaled
  // ONCE, straight to its final size, instead of being crushed to 44px and blown back up.
  desenharHeroiHD(img, alto);

  // O PORTÃO DA HISTÓRIA, SEGUNDA METADE. Daqui para baixo esta função deixa de DESENHAR e
  // passa a MEXER no mundo: a mata nasce e é colhida, o arco do pulo anda, o golpe anda, o pé
  // levanta poeira e o passo soa. Nada disso pode acontecer com uma tela de história aberta —
  // e como `drawHero()` é chamada do caminho de desenho, ela não passa pelo portão do laço de
  // quadro; por isso ele é repetido aqui, lendo a mesma bandeira.
  //
  // Um detalhe que parece bug e não é: se a fala abrir com ela no ar, ela FICA no ar até a
  // tela fechar. Congelar é congelar. A alternativa — deixar o pulo terminar — faria o pouso
  // acontecer sob o texto, com som, baque de câmera e onda de chão, que é justamente o tipo de
  // coisa que este trabalho existe para tirar de cima de quem está lendo.
  if (mundoParado) { lastFi = fi; return; }

  // ...e o portão do MENU, pela mesma razão de estar repetido aqui: a folha nasce e é COLHIDA
  // dentro de `atualizarFolhas` (é ela que soma impacto ao passar por cima), e é a única renda
  // do jogo que não passa pelo laço de quadro. Tudo o mais desta função é o corpo dela — pulo,
  // golpe, poeira do pé — e continua andando, porque a personagem continua andando.
  if (!mundoEmLoop) atualizarFolhas(1 / 60, alto);

  // ---- state advance: identical side effects to the old procedural path ----
  if (air) jumpT--;              // the arc runs down; landing no longer spawns anything
  // A aterrissagem é a passagem de jumpT 1 para 0, e só existe aqui — não há outro lugar no
  // motor que saiba que ela aconteceu.
  if (air && jumpT === 0) {
    somPouso();
    // ONDA 4: o corpo dela CHEGA no chão e o quadro assenta junto (~1 px). Isto é dela,
    // não gramática de combate — vale em qualquer capítulo, como o som do pouso ao lado.
    kickCamera(90); ondaChao(worldX + HX, false);
  }
  if (attackT > 0) attackT--;

  // poeirinha no pé a cada passo. O gatilho é a VOLTA do ciclo, e não "quadro par": com três
  // quadros por passo, o par acendia duas vezes num passo e uma no seguinte.
  if (!air && attackT <= 0 && fi !== lastFi && fi === 0) {
    parts.push({ x: HX - 6, y: GROUND - 3, vx: -24, vy: -10, life: 0.4, c: "#9b8468", grav: 70 });
  }
  // O PASSO SOA NO MESMO EVENTO QUE TROCA O QUADRO — é por isso que ele casa com o pé por
  // construção, e não por ajuste: o quadro já é escolhido pela DISTÂNCIA percorrida, então a
  // cadência do som herda a cadência da passada em qualquer velocidade, de graça.
  //
  // Um ciclo do sprite são DOIS passos (um pé e o outro), então o som sai duas vezes por
  // ciclo: na volta ao quadro 0 e na metade. Um ciclo de três quadros não tem metade inteira,
  // e `n >> 1` dá 1 — que é o quadro certo, o do outro pé.
  //
  // Silencia enquanto uma tela está aberta. Sob a HISTÓRIA isto virou redundante (o mundo
  // parou e esta linha nem é alcançada), mas sob o MENU o mundo segue andando de propósito
  // (ver historiaAberta) e ouvir os passos dela por baixo do menu é ruído.
  if (!air && attackT <= 0 && fi !== lastFi && !telaAberta()) {
    const meio = frames.length >> 1;
    if (fi === 0 || (meio > 0 && fi === meio)) somPasso();
  }
  lastFi = fi;
}

// ---------- SHARED SCENERY GRAMMAR ----------
// Two loops every place on that strip needs, so they belong to the vocabulary and not to
// one scenario: a continuous skyline whose height comes from three sines (never tiles, and
// runs of equal height are merged so a layer is ~40 rects and not 195), and a band of
// vegetation rooted below the horizon line with a sunlit crown and a distance-graded
// outline. Both were written for RUA DO BAIRRO and are unchanged — they are here so that
// PRAÇA COMUNITÁRIA gets the same silhouette language rather than a second copy of it.
function serra(speed, amp, alturaBase, semente, cor, corLuz) {
  let x = 0, alt = -1, ini = 0;
  const altura = function (xx) {
    const wx = (xx + worldX * speed) * 0.6 + semente;
    return Math.max(2, Math.round(alturaBase + amp * (
      0.54 * Math.sin(wx * 0.029) + 0.29 * Math.sin(wx * 0.073 + 1.7) + 0.17 * Math.sin(wx * 0.013 + 4.1))));
  };
  for (x = 0; x <= W; x++) {
    const a = x < W ? altura(x) : -1;
    if (a !== alt) {
      if (alt > 0) {
        cx.fillStyle = cor;
        cx.fillRect(ini, GROUND - 12 - alt, x - ini, alt + 12);
        if (a >= 0 && a < alt) { cx.fillStyle = corLuz; cx.fillRect(ini, GROUND - 12 - alt, x - ini, 2); }
      }
      alt = a; ini = x;
    }
  }
}
// aerial perspective: the far ridge is hazier and lower, the near one darker and taller
function faixaVerde(speed, passo, larg, hMin, hMax, corpo, topo, linha, sem) {
  const q0 = Math.floor(worldX * speed / passo) - 1;
  const n = Math.ceil(W / passo) + 2;
  for (let k = q0; k < q0 + n; k++) {
    const sx = Math.round(k * passo - worldX * speed);
    const th = hMin + Math.floor(hash01(k * sem + 6) * (hMax - hMin));
    const cw = Math.round(larg * 0.7), c0 = sx + ((larg - cw) >> 1);
    if (linha) {                                           // silhouette, one pixel larger
      cx.fillStyle = linha;
      cx.fillRect(sx - 1, GROUND - th - 1, larg + 2, th + 7);
      cx.fillRect(c0 - 1, GROUND - th - 5, cw + 2, 7);
      cx.fillRect(c0 + 1, GROUND - th - 8, cw - 2, 5);
    }
    cx.fillStyle = corpo;
    cx.fillRect(sx, GROUND - th, larg, th + 6);            // the mass, rooted below the line
    cx.fillRect(c0, GROUND - th - 4, cw, 6);               // canopy
    cx.fillRect(c0 + 2, GROUND - th - 7, cw - 4, 4);
    cx.fillStyle = topo;                                   // the sun only reaches the crowns
    cx.fillRect(c0 + 2, GROUND - th - 7, cw - 4, 2);
    cx.fillRect(c0 + cw - 3, GROUND - th - 5, 3, 4);
  }
}

// ---------- CENÁRIOS: THE PLACE YOU ARE IN ----------
// The board's CENÁRIOS strip shows SEVEN places — RUA DO BAIRRO, PRAÇA COMUNITÁRIA, ORLA,
// MATA ATLÂNTICA, CERRADO, CENTRO HISTÓRICO, VILA DA SERRA — and this game had exactly one
// street, hardcoded across `drawScene()` and the palette. A place is now a named thing with
// seven parameters, which are the seven decisions that make one thumbnail on that strip
// different from the next one:
//
//   paleta   — the colour families, as overrides on top of `PALETA_BASE`
//   ceu      — the sky itself: the health ramp, a ramp per hour, the fall to the horizon,
//              the sun, the stars, and the colour distance dissolves into (`CEU_PADRAO`)
//   chaoCor  — the two ends of the ground slab's own gradient
